{"n": 332, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "332.webp", "text": "17 00 039 BLEEDING COOLING SYSTEM\n4/6 Cylinder Models:\n\nLevel of Integrated Expansion Tank - M 40\n\nThis condition is reached relatively easy by keeping to\nthe following procedures when refilling the system (iin\n\n@ workshop).\n\nFilling the System with Simultaneous Bleeding:\n\na) on radiator\nb) on thermostat housing\n(heater open, Ignition on, engine not running)\n\nThe system Is filled until the expansion tank Is\ncompletely filled with coolant and coolant without alr\n\nbubbles runs out of both bleeding points.\n\nTighten bleeder screws.\n\nAlr still trapped In the system will escape when oper-\nating the engine afterwards and cause the coolant\nlevel to drop approximately to the specified mark in\nthe expansion tank (engine speed at least 2500 rpm).\nSlight excessive filling (for example up to the 9th rib\nfram the top) is acceptable.\n\n* Unscrew M 40 bleeder screw.\n\nUnscrew M 20/M 21 bleeder screw.\n\nUnscrew M 40 bleeder screw and walt M 40\n\nuntil coolant “without alr bubbles” runs Mark on tank shows level at about 20\nout. degrees C (68 degrees F).\n\nKeep adding coolant in expansion tank\n\nwhile bleeding.\n\n‘Only use specified coolant*.\n\n2 = Bleeder screw on expansion tank\n\nM 20 (Until 1988 Models)\n\nKeep adding coolant in expansion tank\nwhile bleeding.\n\nMark shows level at 20 degrees C (65\n\ndegrees F).\n‘Only use specified coolant* and **.\n\n* See Service Information of Gr. 00\n“ Source of Supply: HWB\n\n* See Service Information of Gr. 00", "words": [["17", 0.0258, 0.0708, 0.0359, 0.08], ["00", 0.041, 0.0708, 0.0531, 0.0813], ["039", 0.0571, 0.0708, 0.0753, 0.0813], ["BLEEDING", 0.0839, 0.0694, 0.1395, 0.0813], ["COOLING", 0.1436, 0.0694, 0.1951, 0.0813], ["SYSTEM", 0.2002, 0.0694, 0.2457, 0.0813], ["4/6", 0.0238, 0.1045, 0.048, 0.1151], ["Cylinder", 0.0511, 0.1032, 0.0961, 0.1177], ["Models:", 0.1001, 0.1045, 0.1405, 0.1151], ["Level", 0.0248, 0.1376, 0.0531, 0.1481], ["